From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: use Android's daemon platform code on Linux

adbd's privilege handling (should_drop_privileges(), drop_privileges()),
its authentication policy, USB, the --root_seclabel options and the
platform services (root:, unroot:, remount:, reboot:, framebuffer:,
tcpip:, usb:, ...) are only built for Android, so a Linux adbd runs as
whatever started it, never authenticates and offers none of those
services.

Build them on any Linux. Off Android, the build supplies what they
expect underneath (build/platform/): minijail, the AID_SHELL user,
SELinux, and system properties (ro.* from build.prop files, everything
else in a small store under /run), so upstream's logic runs unchanged:
ro.secure, ro.debuggable and service.adb.root decide root, ro.adb.secure
authentication, and `adb root` restarts adbd by exiting, for init to
start it again.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needs the platform layer of a non-Android build]

AI-Generated: Claude Opus 5.5 (Claude Code)
Signed-off-by: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/framebuffer_service.h
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/framebuffer_service.h
@@ -18,6 +18,6 @@
 
 #include "adb_unique_fd.h"
 
-#if defined(__ANDROID__)
+#if defined(__linux__)  // Android, or Linux with build/platform
 void framebuffer_service(unique_fd fd);
 #endif
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/main.cpp
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
